n 0% under an exponent of 2 or 4, and in about 47 to 49% at the band edges 2.5 and 3.5; so the rule rejects surface-law and fourth-power alternatives and is indifferent only at its own pre-registered boundaries. Cross-check (cross_check.py, added 2026-10-31 after the result; verdict unchanged): the collaborator swarm's test of this claim (origin/main, run cursor/claim-tests-thompson-efb7, NHANES 2007-2018, ages 0 to 19.99 with recumbent length under 24 months) reports a pooled individual-level exponent of 2.408 (95% CI 2.399 to 2.416, n = 23540) and 'mixed'. On this test's own sample the individual-level exponent is 2.755 (CI 2.736 to 2.775, n = 9715; males 2.716, females 2.812), within 0.03 of the age-bin values, so the unit of analysis (bins versus individuals) is not the cause. The cause is the age range: the collaborator's own 2-20 year window gives 2.736 (CI 2.723 to 2.750, n = 19714), reproducing this test, while their 0-2 year window gives 2.098 and pulls the pooled exponent below the 2.5 edge of the band both tests pre-registered. The 'supports' verdict is therefore conditional on the scope fixed at pre-registration (ages 2 to 19, standing stature); including infancy in Thompson's 'during growth' makes it 'mixed'. Whether infancy is inside the claim is a reading of the claim, not a measurement.
