ely disappeared'; Otaria byronia's W lies above the lowest terrestrial species (Martes foina). Relative spine height from landmarks includes the neural arch and depends on where the authors placed the spinous-process landmarks; the cetacean values come from a different measurement protocol, so only the within-column ratio WI is compared across datasets. No phylogenetic comparative model was fitted (two pinniped species cannot support one); the Mann-Whitney test treats species as independent. Semi-aquatic carnivorans (otters, mink) retain a terrestrial-grade withers index (1.6-1.7), consistent with Thompson's restriction to animals whose weight is carried by water, but they were excluded from the terrestrial reference set by a decision taken before analysis; including them does not change the result. Gillet et al. label 74 species where the paper reports 73 (one specimen label is spelled 'Feresa_attenuta'); species means were taken as labelled.
