ge classes are sparsely sampled (>= 50 fish required) and trawl gear under-samples the largest fish. The determinate alternative had to be given a specific functional form (quadratic rise to a plateau); a different plateau model could change individual dAIC values. Model selection used AIC on 7-18 age-class means, not individual-level likelihoods. Scope: North Sea marine teleosts only (11 species); Thompson's scope was cold-blooded animals in general. For saithe and cod the oldest well-sampled fish are at only 48-65% of the fitted Linf, i.e. the data do not reach the asymptotic region at all. DATRAS is a live database; the API extract is reproducible only to the extent that ICES does not revise the 2000-2024 records. The 50 file checksums of the extract used are in derived/datras_file_manifest.json and in this file. DATRAS 'Species' names are taken as delivered (AphiaID-based) and no taxonomic harmonisation was done.
